<title>ESTONIA: MICROLINK H1 EXPORTS GROW 3.2 TIMES.</title>
<headline>MICROLINK H1 EXPORTS GROW 3.2 TIMES.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Microlink, the largest computer producer in Estonia, saw its exports grow 3.2 times in the first half of 1997 to 41 million kroons, it said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It exported 85 percent of its exports or 35 million kroons to the other Baltic countries, it added in a statement.</p>
<p>The company's market share in Latvia and Lithuania is ten percent and 15.1 percent in the Baltic region.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn newsroom, +372 6209 201, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
